# Barnaba gateway image - public repository
#
# Written from scratch, NOT copied from the source repository, because of one
# line that must not travel in the other direction.
#
#   Here, config/churches.json is created per deployment and mounted read-only,
#   so it must never be baked into the image. Note that .gitignore protects the
#   commit, not the image: `COPY . .` ignores .gitignore entirely. Those are two
#   separate boundaries and this file is the second one.

node_modules
npm-debug.log
.git
.gitignore
.env
*.md
.DS_Store
test-tools
__tests__
*.test.mjs

# Runtime church whitelist: mounted read-only at run time, never baked in.
# The image ships config/churches.example.json only.
config/churches.json
# Same rule, same reason: mounted at run time, never baked into the image.
config/churchData.json
